{"decision": "CONFIRM", "diagnosis": "Fetch fails with `TRAP: cpu trap asserted` and `FAIL 0xdead` instead of clean NOP progress because `mem_rdata_latched_noshuffle` at picorv32.v:384 is inverted, selecting `mem_rdata_q` on `mem_xfer` and live `mem_rdata` when idle, which feeds wrong/stale data into `mem_rdata_latched` (picorv32.v:386-388) causing illegal decode and trap.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -384,1 +384,1 @@
-	assign mem_rdata_latched_noshuffle = (mem_xfer || LATCHED_MEM_RDATA) ? mem_rdata_q : mem_rdata;
+	assign mem_rdata_latched_noshuffle = (mem_xfer || LATCHED_MEM_RDATA) ? mem_rdata : mem_rdata_q;", "reason": "Diagram shows the fetch rdata path through mem_rdata_q mux into decode/trap, confirming the inverted-select explains the TRAP/FAIL and the swap fixes it."}

